  "observations": [
    "Four-column versus one-column median commitment/cap latency: 5.709 to 2.278 ms (quadratic) and 18.423 to 6.120 ms (wide cubic). Commitment commands fall from 199 to 71 and 465 to 151 respectively.",
    "Query medians remain approximately 0.77-0.78 ms for 33 quadratic queries and 1.35-1.37 ms for four wide cubic queries. Commitment tile width does not change the query geometry.",
    "Retained commitment bytes are independent of tile width: 614368 and 2998240. The wide cubic full LDE would occupy 14417920 bytes, exceeding the fixed 4 MiB allocation ceiling."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are two primitive workloads on one desktop RTX 5080, with five measured samples per geometry. They do not qualify complete CUDA proofs, production performance or transactions per hour.",
    "No optimized CPU performance comparison, V100 execution, distributed worker throughput or board-energy comparison was performed.",
    "Wider tiles reduce command count in these cases but require more scratch. Caller-selected tile geometry, default proving backend and production proof/security parameters remain unchanged.",
    "The full native CUDA PCS, remaining proof stages and worker integration are still incomplete."
  ],
